# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q statement.tex
#
# One warning is suppressed, checked hit by hit on 28 August 2026 rather
# than assumed, with a 100% false-positive rate in this file:
#
#   38  "You should not use punctuation in front of quotes." Each of the 5
#       hits is the final character of a sentence quoted verbatim from the
#       source paper. The punctuation belongs to the quoted text; moving it
#       outside the quotation marks would misquote the source.  (5 hits)
#
# Everything else stays on; the one warning 13 chktex raised on the first
# draft (an uppercase word before a colon) was fixed in the source rather
# than silenced. As of 28 August 2026 the file is clean under this config
# and `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n38
}
